---
title: "Group"
description: "--group-<utility>--<state>: react to an ancestor's state."
section: Modifiers
sectionOrder: 2
order: 2
---

Mark an ancestor `data-ui="group"` and its descendants can respond to its state with the `group-` form: `--opacity: 1; --group-opacity--hover: 0.85`. Any marked ancestor counts, nearest or not.

```html
<article data-ui="card group">
  <img src="…" alt="…" style="--opacity: 1; --group-opacity--hover: 0.85" />
  <a href="/p/1" style="--text: var(--color-muted-foreground); --group-text--hover: var(--color-foreground)">
    Read more
  </a>
</article>
```

The group form exists for every pseudo-class state (`hover`, `active`, `focus-visible`, `focus-within`, `disabled`, `checked`, `open`). `starting` and `stuck` have no group form: the trigger is the element's own first style, or the sticky container.

Named groups (`data-group-name`) are reserved and not implemented.
